title: Motion of No Confidence
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/commons.svg
tags: commons
view-if: no_confidence_timer <= 0 and no_confidence_won = 0 and months_to_election > 2 and con_in_government = 0
on-arrival: no_confidence_timer = 6; month_actions += 1

= Motion of No Confidence

"That this House has no confidence in Her Majesty's Government."

If the motion passes, Callaghan must call an election. If it fails, we look foolish and the government looks stronger. The arithmetic depends on the minor parties.

[? if lib_lab_pact : While the Lib-Lab Pact holds, the Liberals will vote with the government. ?]

[? if devolution_failed = 0 : The SNP still hopes Labour will deliver a Scottish Assembly. ?][? if devolution_failed = 1 : After the referendum fiasco, the SNP has no reason left to keep Labour in office. ?]

- @vote: Table the motion.
- @easy_discard

@vote
title: Table the motion
on-arrival: {!
// ---- count the division ----
// Labour: the Speaker is counted in "other"; two Labour deputy speakers
// don't vote, and one gravely ill Labour MP can't attend.
var noes = Q.lab_mps - 3;
var ayes = Q.con_mps;
var abstain = 0;
// Liberals: free to vote against the government only once the Pact is over.
if (Q.lib_lab_pact == 0 && Q.lib_relation >= 30) {
    ayes += Q.lib_mps;
} else {
    noes += Q.lib_mps;
}
// SNP: turns on Labour if devolution has failed, or if we've courted them.
if (Q.devolution_failed == 1 || Q.snp_relation >= 50) {
    ayes += Q.snp_mps;
} else {
    noes += Q.snp_mps;
}
// Plaid Cymru: usually sustains Labour.
if (Q.pc_relation >= 55) {
    ayes += Q.pc_mps;
} else {
    noes += Q.pc_mps;
}
// Northern Ireland: two nationalist MPs abstain; the ten Unionists split
// according to how far we've won them over.
var unionists = 10;
var frac = (Q.uup_relation - 30) / 40;
if (frac < 0) {
    frac = 0;
} else if (frac > 1) {
    frac = 1;
}
var unionist_ayes = Math.round(unionists * frac);
ayes += unionist_ayes;
noes += unionists - unionist_ayes;
abstain += Q.ni_mps - unionists;
// a dissident or two on our own side if the party is badly split
if (Q.dissent > 0.35) {
    ayes -= 2;
    abstain += 2;
}
Q.nc_ayes = ayes;
Q.nc_noes = noes;
Q.nc_unionist_ayes = unionist_ayes;
Q.nc_passed = (ayes > noes) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: passed if nc_passed = 1; failed if nc_passed = 0

@passed
on-arrival: no_confidence_won = 1; time_to_election = 2; thatcher_rating += 5; dry_dissent -= 5; loyalist_dissent -= 5; right_dissent -= 5; wet_dissent -= 3
call: set_election
achievement: no_confidence

= Ayes [+ nc_ayes +], Noes [+ nc_noes +]

The tellers come to the table, and the Opposition whip is on the right-hand side: we have won. For the first time since 1924, a government has been defeated on a motion of confidence.

Callaghan rises, says the government will take its case to the country, and sits down. The general election is set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@failed
on-arrival: no_confidence_lost += 1; thatcher_rating -= 4; lab_leader_rating += 2; loyalist_dissent += 4; wet_dissent += 4; labour_credibility += 2

= Ayes [+ nc_ayes +], Noes [+ nc_noes +]

The government survives. Callaghan thanks the House with a smile, and the papers ask whether the Opposition can count. [? if nc_unionist_ayes < 8 : We needed more of the Ulster Unionists. ?][? if lib_lab_pact : While the Pact lasts, the Liberals were never going to help. ?]
